- Marital status: Being married may provide social support; divorced status may increase risk of PPD.
- Number of household members: More household members might provide more support or more stress depending on context; generally, fewer household members might increase isolation risk.
- Relationship with husband: Poor or bad relationship with husband increases emotional stress and risk of PPD.
- Addiction: Addiction (smoking, drinking, drugs) may be associated with higher risk of PPD due to underlying stress or coping issues.

